    "chunk_text": "But, yet, there have been requests from a variety of different quarters, particularly from community savings and credit service providers' organizations led by women all over the country. Also, several women\u2019s organizations have made representations to the oversight committee which went into the provisions of this Act and brought to their attention some of the glaring shortcomings. They also sought full exemption for their community savings and for credit service providers, particularly because their organizations are based on membership savings. They lend only to members and are non-profit entities, they do not require collateral and also, they have a cap on interest. So, therefore, they are not like the credit agencies which are charging very exorbitant rates of interest. Therefore, these organizations should be categorized separately and that was their request. But, that request has not been accommodated. That is their principle concern and it has been brought to the notice of the Government by a variety of parties. Even Members of the Government spoke about it, but the Government say that they will bring in some regulations later after the Bill has been enacted. But, that is inadequate.\n\nshould have compassion and courage to stand up against injustice. One fine day when these things happen to us, we would be in a terrible position.\n\nThis is not the first time it happened. When Venezuela\u2019s President Nicolas Maduro was openly abducted after attacking the Capital of Venezuela, this Government said nothing about it. For all this, Venezuela is a country which follows Che Guevara and his principles and you all also started your organization on Che Guevara\u2019s principles. But, now, Sir, they have forgotten about Che Guevara, they have forgotten about Maduro and have totally ignored them. They have become so pally with the capitalist nations."
