    "chunk_text": "presently functioning at this Secretariat. Sri Lanka has also designated senior officers from relevant Ministries and agencies as pillar coordinators, who plan and conduct activities and awareness programmes with the participation of other member States.\n\nWith regard to the location of the permanent Secretariat, while the previous Government had identified the BMICH premises, the present Government has not endorsed that option due to the high recurrent rental costs involved. The current position of the Government is to identify either a Government-owned facility that can be provided free of charge or a more cost-effective alternative location, ensuring fiscal responsibility and sustainability.\n\nIn operational terms, Sri Lanka actively engages in Colombo Security Conclave-related cooperation and information sharing. By way of example, the Sri Lanka Navy maintains close coordination with the Indian Navy on issues such as narcotics trafficking, human smuggling, illegal fishing and other forms of transnational organized crimes. In November, 2024, information shared by Sri Lanka regarding a suspected drug-trafficking fishing vessel led to the interception of the vessel by the Indian Navy and its subsequent handover to Sri Lanka for legal action, demonstrating the practical value of such cooperation.\n\nSri Lanka has also participated in and contributed to a wide range of Colombo Security Conclave-related exercises, workshops, and training programmes. These activities are undertaken in accordance with the Joint Annual Action Plans agreed under the Colombo Security Conclave framework."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-05-2026-03-05",
