    "chunk_size_bytes": 1060,
    "chunk_text": "We know that during the COVID-19 pandemic, work from home was promoted and gradually, people had been asked to come back to work. If we could create a situation where we could get people to work at least two days a week from home, we can encourage more women to join the workforce. So, we need to create a framework that permits women to work from home, encouraging more of them to join the workforce.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0d9c\u0db8\u0dd0\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dd2\u0dbb 2009 \u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc2\u0db1\u0dda \u0dd4\u0d9a\u0dc1\u0db0\u0dd9 \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0da7 \u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dda\u0db1\u0dc3\u0dda after the eradication of the LTTE, 90,000 women have become widows and those 90,000 widows are living under very difficult circumstances. So, I think this Government should take note of that and try to give them\n\n1911 1912\n\n\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dc0\n\na better life through an accelerated social welfare programme. After the conflict, 90,000 have become war-widows in this country. They are a silent lot and nobody seems to talk about them, but there is a lot to be done with regard to them."
