    "chunk_size_bytes": 2024,
    "chunk_text": "\u0dda\u0db6\u0dc4\u0dda\u0db1\u0dc4\u0db8 \u0dc3\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0d9a \u0dba\u0dd20 \u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dba \u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0dda\u0db1\u0dc0\u0db8\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dda \u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d87\u0db8\u0d9a \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db8\u0dc40 \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db8\u0dc4\u0da7 \u0dc0\u0dd2,\u0dc4\u0da9\u0dd2 13\u0d9a \u0d9a\u0dc4\u0dbd \u0d9a\u0dca \u0d9a \u0dda\u0db6,\u0dc0\u0dc40\n\nprovisions exist not as an instrument of control, but as safeguards which enable the State to act decisively in order to maintain stability, protect essential services and ensure the security of our people when circumstances demand preparedness. Today\u2019s discussion must, therefore, be placed within the broader international environment in which Sri Lanka currently operates.\n\nThe world, today, is experiencing a period of heightened geopolitical tension, conflicts and confrontations in different regions and has begun to intersect on critical global trade routes and energy corridors. The rapid escalation of hostilities in the Middle East has raised serious concerns about regional stability and international peace and security. In that context, Sri Lanka has already made its position clear. Our Government has called for utmost restraint and immediate de-escalation, urging all concerned parties to refrain from further provocative actions that would widen the conflict and bring severe humanitarian and economic consequences.\n\nSri Lanka formally believes that diplomacy must prevail over confrontation. Madam, at the heart of these tensions lies a fundamental question about the international system itself, whether the world will continue to be guided by the international law and a rules-based order or whether the stability of regions and sea lanes will increasingly be shaped by confrontation and unilateral action. For countries such as Sri Lanka, the answer to that question is of vital importance."
  },
