    "description": "Hansard of 2026-03-06",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23376_english_2026-03-06.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-06-2026-03-06-0212",
    "chunk_index": 212,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "189d95f6d745d9f3a26fa778870d9f6b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1979,
    "chunk_text": "Last year, you mentioned that we were supposed to get US Dollars 891 million, but I do not see that that mount has physically come into this country. So, Madam, I would emphasize in this House at this moment that the Government must take that opportunity. Hon. Prime Minister, ensure that you all fly to the Middle East and get down investments. It is not a bomb that fell just into Iran. Whether it be Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Kuwait, Jordan, Lebanon or Cyprus, all those countries have been engulfed in a situation where there is a protracted war going on.\n\n2073 2074\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dc4,\u0dc4 \u0d9a \u0db8\u0db1\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dc4]\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 06\n\nwhich Sri Lanka is unable to disentangle itself from to be a good selling point.\n\nSo, I would take this opportunity to remind the Government that this is an opportunity we could seize. We must ensure that we get investments financially as well as physical investments to Sri Lanka. The IMF wants us to pay US Dollars 6 billion in debt servicing in 2028. That is what you all have got through the process of agreements. But, tell the IMF that this is an opportunity and that we want incentives for qualifying for payments to get investments. The Managing Director of the IMF, Ms. Kristalina Georgieva came to Sri Lanka last week. Ensure that we basically tell them, \u201cThere is a problem in the Middle East. Please ensure that we get incentive qualifications so that we could attract investments into this country.\" Since there is a time constraint, I call upon the Hon. Prime Minister, who is seated there at this moment, to tell the Government to get the IMF to give you that benefit because this Agreement is effective only till the end of this year. Then, by March, 2027, we have to start paying and the opportunity for Sri Lanka reduces. So, we have to give incentives to get investments into the country. By the time, construction comes, you need not ask the IMF to give it, but you could basically take it on."
  },
